  (text
    "PI7C9X3G606GP (Diodes DS43484 Rev5-2) - ball map transcribed from section 3; all 144 balls placed (power/GND balls drawn stacked).\nPORTCFG[2:0]=101 -> 6-port/6-lane mode (Table 5-1). Lane map (Table 5-4): L0=P0 upstream, L1=P1, L2=P4, L3=P5, L4=P6, L5=P7.\nSlot1 = lane1/P1 (REFCLKO1, CLKREQ_L1), Slot2 = lane2/P4 (REFCLKO4, CLKREQ_L4), Slot3 = lane3/P5 (REFCLKO5, CLKREQ_L5). P6/P7 unused (NC).\nCKMODE=0 (BASE): REFCLK0 from host via edge; REFCLKP/N1 tied to GND (Table 5-5).\nStraps: CHIPMODE=00 (330R PD), CKMODE 330R PD, TEST 330R PD, TMS/TRST_L 330R PD, HOT_PLUG_EN_L=1 (5.1k PU), PM_L11_EN_L=1 (L1.1 off; 330R PD option DNP).\nEdge connector (add-in-card side, fed from ADT-Link M41 M.2->x1 riser): B14/B15 = host TX -> switch RX (no caps); switch TX -> 220nF -> A16/A17.\nEdge +12V/+3.3V/3.3Vaux NOT used (carrier is powered from its own 12V input). SMBus/JTAG/WAKE# on edge left open.\nPERST# from edge -> SN74LVC1G07 (VCC 1.8V, 5V-tolerant input) -> PERST_L; also fans out (3.3V) to per-slot AND gates.\nVERIFY: HCSL termination (series 0R + DNP 49.9R shunts placed), PDC_L behaviour with hot-plug disabled (DNP 0R to GND option),\nunused SerDes lane handling, decoupling/bead values - Diodes HW design guide / eval board schematic not public: request from Diodes FAE.\nI2C slave (default addr 0x6F) behind PCA9306 (1.8V <-> 3.3V). SPI EEPROM optional config (EEPROM signature 0x1516)."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 400 470 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "3f4c8291-d808-5f23-a1a2-bb50f34e886a"))
